    title: 'Small businesses', eyebrow: 'For teams without a content department', promise: 'Stay visible every week without turning marketing into a second job.', description: 'Framewise replaces the repetitive content routine around research, scripting, generation and uploading. Your team sets the audience, goals, volume and budget once; the engine keeps the pipeline moving.', problem: 'Regular video works, but the work resets every week: find a topic, decide an angle, write the script, create the asset, upload it and remember to do it again.', outcomes: ['Product, customer problem and audience interests drive every search.', 'Selling, informative and entertaining ideas follow your chosen ratio.', 'Opportunity scoring directs generation budget toward stronger ideas first.', 'A dollar balance and monthly budget keep automation financially bounded.'], workflow: [{ title: 'Connect the business', text: 'Start with the existing website instead of writing a new creative brief from scratch.' }, { title: 'Balance the plan', text: 'Choose how much content should sell, inform or entertain and how many videos should ship each week.' }, { title: 'Automate production', text: 'The system creates complete scripts and videos in the format best suited to each idea.' }, { title: 'Publish and learn', text: 'Connected channels receive finished work and measured response influences future research without overfitting.' }], examples: ['Local and professional services', 'SaaS and online products', 'Consumer brands', 'Founder-led small teams'],
